+Version: aider 0.86.2
+
+Task Description:
+## Context
+
+#106 / PR #127 attempted the corpus audit and recorded it as unexecutable: the rule was absent from the checkout and the local build was blocked by a Coursier cache lock at `~/Library/Caches/Coursier/v1/.structure.lock`. That report itself says: "Once the rule is available, rerun this audit". #129 makes the rule available; this task is that rerun.
+
+This is the only step that exercises the whole chain on code nobody wrote as a fixture: candidate extraction over real project sources, normalizer, Cats index lookup, ranking, rendering.
+
+## Goal
+
+Run `PreferCatsFunctions` in check mode over the four local Typelevel repos and produce an audited hit/decline report.
+
+## Scope
+
+1. Run the rule against `/Users/viktorskalinins/IdeaProjects/my/gh-tasks-llm-executor`, `/Users/viktorskalinins/IdeaProjects/my/arrowstep`, `/Users/viktorskalinins/IdeaProjects/my/cctv-analyzer-scala`, `/Users/viktorskalinins/IdeaProjects/my/ScalaSemanticMCP`.
+2. Replace the placeholder `## Corpus run` section of `docs/PREFER_CATS_FUNCTIONS.md` with the real results, per repo.
+3. Audit every proposed rewrite individually.
+4. Aggregate declines by reason.
+5. Leave the corpus repos unmodified.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. The `## Corpus run` table in `docs/PREFER_CATS_FUNCTIONS.md` has one row per repo whose "Proposed rewrites" cell is an integer (0 allowed) or the literal word `skipped` followed by the quoted build error text — the string `n/a - rule unavailable` must no longer appear anywhere in the file.
+2. Every proposed rewrite has its own audit line carrying the source location and exactly one verdict from {correct, false-positive, unclear}; each `false-positive` line links a filed follow-up issue referencing #34.
+3. Declines are aggregated as counts per reason, each reason being one of the decline rules D1/D2/D3/D4 from `docs/PREFER_CATS_FUNCTIONS.md` section 3.
+4. `git status --porcelain` in each of the four corpus repos shows no new or modified tracked file attributable to this run (pre-existing working-tree changes are left untouched and noted).
+5. No change is made to `scalafix/src/fix/PreferCatsFunctions.scala` or `scalafix/src/fix/prefercats/` in this task; behavior problems found are filed as follow-up issues instead.
+
+## Notes / Risks
+
+- If the Coursier cache lock error recurs, fix or work around it (clear the stale lock / point `COURSIER_CACHE` elsewhere) rather than recording the run as blocked a second time.
+- A repo that genuinely cannot build is `skipped` with the quoted error — that satisfies criterion 1, an unattempted repo does not.
+
+Task metadata:
